 One tarball, several vendors, several licences -- this file is a defensible
 aggregate, NOT a fully-verified per-file audit. See
 core/rpm/indi-stable-3rdparty-libs.spec's own License: comment for exactly
 which licences were read in full text versus inferred, and DESIGN.md, "The
 licence tiers", for why astroasis/atik/qhy/svbony/pentax/qsi are NOT in
 this package at all. Fishcamp was in that list too until 2026-08-27, when
 its licence was confirmed clear -- see DESIGN.md, "QSI and Fishcamp
 resolved".

